    {
      "id": "tvjms65",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Integrated Pest Management (IPM)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wio68ee",
      "content": "Integrated Pest Management (IPM) is an ecosystem-based strategy that focuses on long-term prevention of pests through biological control, habitat manipulation, resistant varieties, and use of pesticides only when necessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "cq27n64",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Components of IPM"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "IPM principles and individual components are major recurring topics in agricultural competitive exams.",
        "Expect questions regarding pesticide classification according to their specific mode of action.",
        "Types of insect metamorphosis and major crop pest identifications are frequently tested."
      ],
      "id": "7mfbmtr"
    },
    {
      "id": "h0kcr9t",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Deep summer ploughing, crop rotation, trap crops, proper spacing, destruction of crop residue: </strong>Cultural Control",
        "<strong>Hand-picking, light traps, sticky traps, pheromone traps, bird perches: </strong>Mechanical Control",
        "<strong>Trichogramma (egg parasitoid), Chrysoperla (lacewing predator), Coccinella, NPV, Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt): </strong>Biological Control",
        "<strong>Last resort; selective pesticides; correct dose and timing; avoid broad-spectrum: </strong>Chemical Control",
        "<strong>Use of resistant varieties; most sustainable approach: </strong>Host Plant Resistance (HPR)",
        "<strong>Plant Quarantine Act; import/export restrictions; pest-free certification: </strong>Regulatory Control"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bcqejpv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Pesticide Classification by Mode of Action"
    },
    {
      "id": "4thqepa",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Class</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Examples</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Organochlorines (OC)</p>",
            "<p>Nerve toxin (disrupts Na channels)</p>",
            "<p>DDT, Endosulfan (banned), Lindane — mostly banned now</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Organophosphates (OP)</p>",
            "<p>Inhibit AChE (acetylcholinesterase)</p>",
            "<p>Chlorpyrifos, Monocrotophos, Dimethoate, Profenophos</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Carbamates</p>",
            "<p>Inhibit AChE (reversible)</p>",
            "<p>Carbaryl (Sevin), Carbofuran, Methomyl</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pyrethroids</p>",
            "<p>Disrupt Na channels (fast knockdown)</p>",
            "<p>Cypermethrin, Deltamethrin, Lambda-cyhalothrin, Permethrin</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Neonicotinoids</p>",
            "<p>Act on nicotinic acetylcholine receptors</p>",
            "<p>Imidacloprid, Thiamethoxam, Clothianidin — systemic</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bt toxins (Biological)</p>",
            "<p>Disrupt midgut membrane; Lepidoptera-specific</p>",
            "<p>Bt formulations; Bt cotton (Cry1Ac gene)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Spinosyns</p>",
            "<p>Acts on nicotinic receptor and GABA receptor</p>",
            "<p>Spinosad, Spinetoram — derived from Saccharopolyspora spinosa</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>IGRs (Insect Growth Regulators)</p>",
            "<p>Disrupt moulting (chitin inhibitors) or juvenile hormone mimics</p>",
            "<p>Diflubenzuron, Buprofezin, Lufenuron</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
